            <ArticleTitle>A metal-lustrous porphyrin foil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10703-10706</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06159e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A metal-lustrous self-standing film, named &quot;porphyrin foil&quot;, was formed from a glass-forming polymeric porphyrin. The amorphous glass nature of the porphyrin foil played a key role in spontaneously producing a smooth surface. Its sharp contrast in intense absorption and specular reflection of light at each wavelength provided a brilliant metallic lustre.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
